  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 138 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nWhile high pressure remains centered over the southern Great\nPlains the next seven days, upper ridging over West Texas and \neastern New Mexico weakens and flow becomes more southeasterly\nallowing for slightly cooler and more moist air to advect into the\narea. Highs drop down into the mid 90s next week which is a\nwelcome relief to recent heat though still a few degrees above\nnormal. The NBM may be underestimating rain chances next week,\nespecially in the higher elevations west of the Pecos River when\ndaytime heating combines with better moisture to produce afternoon\nshowers and storms.\n\nThe extended period is interesting looking west into the Pacific.\nModels are showing a trough in the western United States becoming\nstationary and possibly pulling in moisture from east Pac tropical\nsystems across northern Mexico and into our CWA. Confidence is low\nin increasing rain chances next weekend, but it will be something\nto keep an eye on.\n\nHennig",
